{
 "id": "P16",
 "kind": "echarts",
 "title": "GLM-5.3 has cheaper tokens than Sonnet but uses 3x as many",
 "section": "recommendations",
 "order": 10,
 "caption": "Each dot is one monitor setting: what it paid per million tokens, input and output together (across), and how many tokens it used per program (up). Cost per program is the product, so dots on one diagonal cost the same. Prices are the list prices behind P01.",
 "notes": [
  "GLM-5.3 at max costs 1.6x Sonnet per program although its tokens cost about half as much: the difference is volume, mostly hidden reasoning (M20). Sonnet being cheaper per program needs no subsidy to explain it.",
  "Haiku 4.5 uses about as many tokens as Haiku 5.5 but its list price per token is ten times higher, so it costs 7.2x Haiku 5.5's default per program and catches fewer backdoors.",
  "List prices change; tokens per program don't. Reporting both lets anyone reprice these results later."
 ],
